// ============================================================================
// perm_entropy.kn — TurboKain 23: Fast Permutation Entropy & LZW Complexity
// Non-Linear Dynamic Systems & Model-Free Technosignature Screener
//
// Theoretical Foundation:
//   Standard Fourier and incoherent dedoppler tools assume periodic tones or
//   linear drift lines, remaining blind to flat-spectrum digital modulations,
//   spread-spectrum communications (DSSS/FHSS), chaotic attractors, and
//   non-linear physical emissions.
//
//   perm_entropy operates directly on time-series voltages without spectral
//   assumptions by evaluating the phase space ordinal trajectory:
//     1. Permutation Entropy H_PE(tau): 5D delay embedding mapped via Lehmer code
//        to 120 factoradic bins. Thermal Gaussian noise yields H_PE ~ 1.000;
//        structured signals cause an instantaneous collapse in ordinal entropy.
//     2. Jensen-Shannon Statistical Complexity C_JS: Locates signals on the
//        Rosso et al. (2007) Complexity-Entropy plane. Separates trivial noise
//        (C ~ 0) and simple periodic tones (C < 0.2) from complex non-linear
//        modulations / chaotic dynamics (C >= 0.150).
//     3. Lempel-Ziv Algorithmic Complexity K_LZ: Kaspar-Schuster LZ76 parsing
//        over binarized trajectory measuring rate of new pattern generation.
//        Thermal noise yields K_LZ ~ 1.04; structured codes collapse K_LZ << 1.0.
//
// Semantics & Decision Ladder:
//   * L3 converge: lehmer5 ordinal factoradic mapping verified with random(8) fuzz.
//   * L2 law: pe_bounds, complexity_bounds, lz_bounds, anomaly_verdict.
//   * L1 world/patch: EntropyAuthority ↔ EntropyMirror tracking streaming audits.
//   * Memory: Zero-allocation hot loops, +32 byte SIMD padding, single decay.
//
// Exit codes: 0 searched, 1 help / prove FAIL, 2 error.
// ============================================================================

